# CODEOWNERS requests a review from the listed owner(s) whenever a pull
# request touches a matching path. See
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Workflow files run with the repository's own GITHUB_TOKEN and (for
# `pull_request`-triggered workflows) are read from the pull request's own
# merge ref -- so a pull request could otherwise change what a check does,
# or what a workflow is allowed to do. This requests a maintainer review on
# any change here; it does not by itself require one -- the branch ruleset
# does not mandate code-owner review, that's a separate maintainer decision.
# Outside contributors' workflow runs already wait for maintainer approval
# on every run (not just the first), so a workflow edit is seen before it
# ever runs, and merging still needs one approving review either way.
